IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `on-ow`
IMPORT `on-ow-dates`

-- Ontario Works Act, 1997 and O. Reg. 134/98 -- the applicant's or recipient's questions: "Can I apply on my own behalf?
-- What is my asset limit? What are my monthly budgetary requirements? How much of my earnings counts? Am I eligible? How
-- much assistance a month? By when must I ask for an internal review, and appeal?" Every question calls the rules in
-- on-ow.l4 and on-ow-dates.l4; nothing is restated. Plain inputs, one per fact the person can state.
-- © King's Printer for Ontario, 1997 and 1998. NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Can I apply for Ontario Works`

@export Can I apply for Ontario Works income assistance on my own behalf under O. Reg. 134/98 s 11 (1) and (3)?
GIVEN `I am a dependent adult of a parent I live with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are 18 or older, live with your parent, and are a dependent adult of that parent's benefit unit (not financially independent, and not on ODSP)
      `I live with my parent and am not financially independent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live with a parent and none of the s 2 (2) tests of financial independence fits you (for example: you have never lived with a spouse, never been self-supporting or on assistance for two years in all, never lived away from your parents since 18, are not five years out of school, have no college diploma or university degree, never had custody of your child)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply on my own behalf` IF
    `may apply on his or her own behalf` `I am a dependent adult of a parent I live with` `I live with my parent and am not financially independent`

§ `What is my asset limit`

@export What is the limit on my benefit unit's assets for Ontario Works under O. Reg. 134/98 s 38 (1)?
GIVEN `I have a spouse in my benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a spouse (married, common-law, or someone you have lived with for three months in a relationship like a couple) is included in your benefit unit
      `my adult dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your (or your spouse's) children aged 18 or older who live with you and depend on you are in your benefit unit
      `my dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children under 18 who live with you, and for whom you or your spouse get the Canada child benefit, are in your benefit unit
      `I or my spouse have applied for ODSP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse has applied for income support under the Ontario Disability Support Program and the application is not yet decided (not covered)
      `I am applying only on behalf of my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying only on behalf of your dependent child because you cannot apply on your own behalf (s 11 (2), (4); not covered)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my asset limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I or my spouse have applied for ODSP`
            THEN `not covered` `an applicant for ODSP takes the ODSP asset limit (s 38 (2)), which is not encoded`
        IF `I am applying only on behalf of my child`
            THEN `not covered` `assistance on behalf of a dependent child only (s 11 (2), (4); s 38 (1) (e)) is not encoded`
        OTHERWISE
            `answered` (`the prescribed limit for assets` (`Benefit unit` WITH `has a spouse included` IS `I have a spouse in my benefit unit`, `dependent adults` IS `my adult dependants`, `dependent children` IS `my dependent children`))

§ `What are my monthly budgetary requirements`

@export What are my benefit unit's monthly budgetary requirements for Ontario Works under O. Reg. 134/98 s 41 (1) and s 42 (basic needs, shelter and allowances)?
GIVEN `I have a spouse in my benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a spouse is included in your benefit unit
      `my adult dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent adults (your or your spouse's children 18 or older living with you and depending on you) are in your benefit unit
      `my dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children under 18 are in your benefit unit
      `I get board and lodging, or live in a long-term care home, hostel or community residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive board and lodging from the same source, or live in a long-term care home, an emergency hostel or a funded community residence (not covered)
      `a child in my unit is in shared custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any child in your benefit unit is in shared custody (you get the Canada child benefit as a shared-custody parent, or share physical custody about equally; not covered)
      `I am a sponsored immigrant living with my sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member of your unit is a sponsored immigrant living in the sponsor's home or accommodation (not covered)
      `I live north of the 50th parallel without year round road access` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live north of the 50th parallel in a place without year-round road access
      `my monthly shelter cost` IS A NUMBER @desc Your actual monthly shelter cost for your principal residence: rent (not parking or cable), or mortgage principal and interest, property taxes, home insurance, condominium fees, and utilities and heat not included in rent, in dollars
      `of which my monthly cost of heat` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of that monthly shelter cost that is the cost of energy for heat, in dollars (0 if heat is included in rent)
      `my special diet amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The special diet amount the administrator determined for you for a listed medical condition, in dollars a month (0 if none)
      `my spouse's special diet amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The special diet amount determined for your spouse, in dollars a month (0 if none)
      `members aged 65 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of your benefit unit are 65 or older
      `members pregnant or breast-feeding on a non-dairy diet` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are pregnant, or breast-feeding an infant under 12 months, and have a health professional's confirmation that they need a non-dairy diet
      `other members pregnant or breast-feeding` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other members are pregnant, or breast-feeding an infant under 12 months, as confirmed by a health professional
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What are my budgetary requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I get board and lodging, or live in a long-term care home, hostel or community residence`
            THEN `not covered` `board and lodging, a long-term care home, a hostel or a community residence (O. Reg. 134/98 ss 43, 44) is not encoded`
        IF `a child in my unit is in shared custody`
            THEN `not covered` `a child in shared custody halves the child's amounts (s 44.2), which is not encoded`
        IF `I am a sponsored immigrant living with my sponsor`
            THEN `not covered` `a sponsored immigrant living with the sponsor (s 51) is not encoded`
        OTHERWISE
            LET `unit` MEANS `Benefit unit` WITH `has a spouse included` IS `I have a spouse in my benefit unit`, `dependent adults` IS `my adult dependants`, `dependent children` IS `my dependent children`
                `facts` MEANS `Allowance facts` WITH
                    `north of the 50th parallel without road access` IS `I live north of the 50th parallel without year round road access`
                    `actual shelter cost`                           IS `my monthly shelter cost`
                    `cost of energy for heat`                       IS `of which my monthly cost of heat`
                    `special diet amounts`                          IS LIST `my special diet amount`, `my spouse's special diet amount`
                    `members 65 or older`                           IS `members aged 65 or older`
                    `members pregnant or breast-feeding needing a non-dairy diet` IS `members pregnant or breast-feeding on a non-dairy diet`
                    `other members pregnant or breast-feeding`      IS `other members pregnant or breast-feeding`
            IN  `answered` (`the budgetary requirements under s 41` `unit` `facts`)

§ `How much of my income counts`

@export How much of my benefit unit's monthly income counts for Ontario Works under O. Reg. 134/98 ss 48 and 49, after the earnings exemptions?
GIVEN `our gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The total gross monthly earnings from employment, training payments and net self-employment income of all adult members of your benefit unit (not children under 18 or full-time secondary students, whose earnings are exempt), in dollars
      `deductions from our pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The deductions from that pay required by law or the terms of employment for income tax, CPP, EI, union dues or pension contributions, in dollars a month
      `adults with earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many adult members of your unit have earnings
      `licensed child care we pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Monthly child care costs you pay to a licensed child care provider or a school board's extended day program, not reimbursed, needed so you can work or take part in employment activities, in dollars
      `other child care we pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Monthly child care costs you pay to anyone else (not a member of your unit), not reimbursed, in dollars
      `children in other child care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children those other child care costs are for (each is capped at $600 a month)
      `our other monthly income` IS A NUMBER @desc All other monthly income of your unit that is not exempt: for example EI, CPP, WSIB, support payments, pensions. Leave out the Canada child benefit, Ontario child benefit, GST/HST credit, Canada workers benefit, Ontario Trillium Benefit and Canada disability benefit, which are exempt
      `I am applying or in my first three months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying for assistance, or are in your first three months of receiving it (the $200 and 50% earnings exemptions do not apply then)
      `I was on assistance recently with earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received Ontario Works or ODSP continuously for at least three months, it was cancelled less than six months before this application, and you had earnings when it was cancelled (the exemptions then apply at once)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my income counts` MEANS
    LET `earnings` MEANS `Earnings facts` WITH
            `gross monthly earnings`                   IS `our gross monthly earnings`
            `deductions required by law or employment` IS `deductions from our pay`
            `adult members with earnings`              IS `adults with earnings`
            `child care expenses allowed`              IS `the child care expenses allowed` `licensed child care we pay` `other child care we pay` `children in other child care`
        `exemptions` MEANS `the earnings exemptions apply` `I am applying or in my first three months` `I was on assistance recently with earnings`
    IN  `the income of the benefit unit` (`the earnings included in income` `earnings` `exemptions`) `our other monthly income`

§ `Am I eligible, and how much would I get`

@export Am I eligible for Ontario Works income assistance under s 7 (3) of the Ontario Works Act, 1997 and O. Reg. 134/98?
GIVEN `I live in Ontario` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are resident in Ontario
      `I can apply on my own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you may apply on your own behalf (see the first question)
      `my budgetary requirements` IS A NUMBER @desc Your benefit unit's monthly budgetary requirements, in dollars (see the budgetary requirements question)
      `my income that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc Your benefit unit's monthly income that counts, in dollars (see the income question, answered as an applicant)
      `our assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of your benefit unit's assets, leaving out your home, one motor vehicle, tools of the trade, RESPs, RDSPs, a prepaid funeral and the other items exempt under s 39 (1), in dollars
      `my asset limit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your benefit unit's asset limit, in dollars (see the asset limit question)
      `we give the information asked and meet the other conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your dependants provide the identification, financial and other information and verification required, and meet the other prescribed conditions (participation agreement, pursuing other income such as EI or support)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for Ontario Works` IF
        `I can apply on my own behalf`
    AND `is eligible for income assistance under s 7 (3)` `I live in Ontario` `my budgetary requirements` `my income that counts` `our assets` `my asset limit` `we give the information asked and meet the other conditions`

@export How much Ontario Works income assistance would my benefit unit get a month under O. Reg. 134/98 s 40 (1), if eligible?
GIVEN `my budgetary requirements` IS A NUMBER @desc Your benefit unit's monthly budgetary requirements, in dollars (see the budgetary requirements question)
      `my income that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc Your benefit unit's monthly income that counts, in dollars (see the income question)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much Ontario Works a month` MEANS
    `the amount of income assistance` `my budgetary requirements` `my income that counts`

§ `If I disagree with a decision` -- for a person who has received a decision they want reviewed

@export By what date must I request an internal review of an Ontario Works decision under O. Reg. 134/98 s 69 (1)?
GIVEN `the day I received the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you received (or are deemed to have received) the written decision
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I request an internal review` MEANS `the last day to request an internal review` `the day I received the decision`

@export By what date must I appeal to the Social Benefits Tribunal under O. Reg. 134/98 s 72 (1) and (2)?
GIVEN `the day the decision became final` IS A DATE @desc The day the administrator's decision became final after the internal review (the decision on internal review, or the end of the review period)
      `the date of the original decision` IS A DATE @desc The date of the administrator's original decision
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I appeal` MEANS `the last day to appeal to the Tribunal` `the day the decision became final` `the date of the original decision`
